16 |     let $k: i32[unit: length.kilometers] = $m as i32[unit: length.kilometers];
   |                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 what: this goes to a unit 1000 times bigger, which can lose something, so `as` says how it rounds
 why:  a value changes unit with `as`: a float rounds to the nearest, an integer going to a smaller unit is exact, and one going to a bigger unit says how it rounds with `as.trunc`, `as.floor` or `as.exact` (D255)
